# NEG (Round XXV Track B — one-sided-combinator class): Option.unwrap_error
# does NOT exist in the phase-0 subset. Ratified Result-only per
# `docs/language-reference.md:3861-3891` (Option has one payload; no Error
# to unwrap).
#
# Pre-fix (RED-verified 2026-08-02): Rust `gg check` prints "OK: no semantic
# errors" then `gg build` crashes at C-compile with
# `'__gg_Option__int64_t' has no member named 'None_0'; did you mean
# 'Some_0'?` inside `Option__int64_t__unwrap_error` (the lowerer emits
# `return __src.None_0;` for a nonexistent Error axis); ggdef `run`
# REJECTED at eval-time via the WEAKER generic fallthrough
# ("`.unwrap_error()` on enum") that doesn't carry the ratified reject
# code — too late for corpus_b `CheckFails` adjudication and imprecise.
# Core #8 both-wrong class.
#
# Post-fix: ggdef `elaborate_method` REJECTS at elaborate-time with
# `error[E_NoMethodFound]: `.unwrap_error()` on Option is outside the
# phase-0 subset (Result-only)` (XXV Track B). Rust `typecheck` REJECTS
# with `error[E_NoMethodFound]: no method `unwrap_error` found on type
# `Option[int] — `.unwrap_error()` is outside the phase-0 subset
# (Result-only)`` via the `reject_wrong_receiver_combinator` chokepoint
# (Round XXVI Track A).

void main():
    Option[int] o = Some(5)
    int x = o.unwrap_error()
    print(x)
